---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="History — Domaine d'Aubigny"
  description="Two thousand years on the same land. From Roman occupation to the Cistercians, a history of wine and terroir."
  lang="en"
>
  <style>
    .history { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: clamp(56px, 12vw, 96px) var(--pad-x); }
    .history__title { font-size: 36px; font-weight: 400; margin-bottom: 48px; }
    .history__section { margin-bottom: 56px; }
    .history__section h2 { font-size: 28px; font-weight: 400; margin-bottom: 20px; }
    .history__section p { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--body); margin-bottom: 16px; }
  </style>

  <section class="history">
    <h1 class="history__title">History & Archives</h1>

    <div class="history__section">
      <h2>Two Thousand Years</h2>
      <p>The lands of Aubigny have been farmed continuously since Roman times. Archaeological evidence—a Gallo-Roman stele preserved at the site—testifies to occupation and viticulture as early as the 1st century AD.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="history__section">
      <h2>The Cistercians, 1132</h2>
      <p>In 1132, Cistercian monks from Cluny established a monastery and vineyards here. The same terroir that suited their purposes then continues to produce exceptional wines today. The lineage is unbroken.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="history__section">
      <h2>Archives</h2>
      <p>Medieval charters, deeds of ownership, and technical records spanning centuries are preserved at the estate. These documents form a complete archive of land use, viticultural practice, and terroir understanding.</p>
      <p>Selected transcriptions and translations are published here, creating an open library of the estate's history.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
